Use __declspec for the Windows DLL linkage

Upstream's bzlib.h cannot be used to link against a bzip2 DLL in the ordinary
way. It defaults to BZ_EXPORT unless BZ_IMPORT is defined, so a consumer that
forgets -DBZ_IMPORT gets export semantics; and on the import side it declares
BZ_API(func) as (WINAPI * func) with an empty BZ_EXTERN, which is a function
*pointer* declaration meant to be filled in with GetProcAddress.

Ice links the bzip2 import library and calls BZ2_bzBuffToBuffCompress and
BZ2_bzBuffToBuffDecompress directly, so it needs plain function declarations.
This flips the default to BZ_IMPORT, so the DLL build opts into exporting with
-DBZ_EXPORT while consumers get import semantics by default, and uses
__declspec(dllexport)/__declspec(dllimport) instead of the function-pointer
scheme.

Do not replace this with a .def file: on Win32 the exported names of these
__stdcall functions depend on how they are exported, and ZeroC.Bzip2 has
shipped this ABI since 2017.

Taken verbatim from the bzlib.h hunks of zeroc-ice/bzip2 commit a549df837
("Add MSVC support", 2017-02-08), the source of every ZeroC.Bzip2 package
published so far. Applies unchanged to bzip2 1.0.6 and 1.0.8.

diff --git a/bzlib.h b/bzlib.h
index 8277123..32d83bb 100644
--- a/bzlib.h
+++ b/bzlib.h
@@ -66,8 +66,8 @@ typedef
    bz_stream;


-#ifndef BZ_IMPORT
-#define BZ_EXPORT
+#ifndef BZ_EXPORT
+#define BZ_IMPORT
 #endif

 #ifndef BZ_NO_STDIO
@@ -83,11 +83,11 @@ typedef
 #   endif
 #   ifdef BZ_EXPORT
 #   define BZ_API(func) WINAPI func
-#   define BZ_EXTERN extern
+#   define BZ_EXTERN __declspec(dllexport)
 #   else
    /* import windows dll dynamically */
-#   define BZ_API(func) (WINAPI * func)
-#   define BZ_EXTERN
+#   define BZ_API(func) WINAPI  func
+#   define BZ_EXTERN __declspec(dllimport)
 #   endif
 #else
 #   define BZ_API(func) func
